 us in mitigating this issue  there's hardly anything that directly  impacts the performance of a vehicle's  engine than overheating and to achieve  Peak condition there has to be a proper  thermal management system within that  vehicle both the motors and the battery  pack have to remain cool in the first  generation of the Tesla Model S and  after just a few quarter mile runs the  vehicle's power would be drastically  throttled down to protect its battery  and motors from overheating however  every iteration of the model S leading  up to the Plaid has seen improvements in  its thermal management system we also  have the latest and greatest in heat  pump which is the basically the HVAC  system for the car it's 30 better cold  weather range and requires 50 less  energy for cabin Heating and freezing  conditions yeah so it's you'll see very  little degradation in cold weather Elon  also speaks about the radiator which is  two times as big as its previous  iterations and he also says that it's  one of the defining factors why the  Plaid can go from 0 to 60 over and over  again without burning up now I might  have hinted at it at the beginning of  this video but I think it's time we  properly addressed it just how fast is  the Tesla plaid Model S I mean is it an  insane engine if it doesn't give the car  insane speed understanding the  impressive speed of the Plaid requires a  quick trip down Tesla's past we need to  First compare this Beast to its previous  iterations June 2012 after years of  waiting the original model S is finally  released and to the Delight of Tesla  customers the world over it is a twin  motor all-wheel luxury vehicle capable  of moving from 0 to 60 mph in 4 0.2  seconds that kind of speed wasn't meant  to be found on an EV in 2012. so driving  a Model S at the time was not too  different from fighting in the American  Civil War with nuclear weapons but Tesla  wasn't done not yet they began dishing  out upgrades with the enthusiasm of a  granny s